= The Orgesch

On 9 May, in Regensburg, the Bavarian forester Georg Escherich founds the Organisation Escherich. It is to unite the civil guards of the whole Reich into one armed league of property owners. They have hundreds of thousands of rifles, and some field guns, hidden on estates and in parish halls. The Allies demand that Germany disarm them, and the government says it is trying.

- @expose: Publish the locations of their depots.
- @campaign: Campaign with the unions for a law to disarm them.

@expose
subtitle: Some depots will be raided. The nationalists will call us informers for Paris.
on-arrival: civil_guards_strength -= 60; repression += 3

*Die Rote Fahne* prints a list of farms, monasteries and sawmills, with the number of machine guns at each. The paper is banned for a week.

@campaign
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Slower. It brings the unions closer.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids a common campaign with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.civil_guards_strength -= 30;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Our resolution passes in union branches across the Reich. In August the Reichstag passes a disarmament law, and Bavaria ignores it.
